  "behavior": [
    "Manual sparse hardware writes use the existing reference native core at timeline.generatedFrames. Existing scheduled and queued PCM is retained; no duplicate voice is substituted for playing-channel input.",
    "Timeline peek observes the producer without advancing the heard cursor. Manual control drafts respond immediately, while sent-register Live/readout follows heard frames. Auto Off acknowledges a deliberate edit once its frame is heard, then remains Off.",
    "Volume, balance, Wave RAM, Noise and fixed CH2-to-CH1 LFO settings preserve untouched bytes/fields. Invalid fields and unknown protected bits reject before any write. Software Envelope, PCM assets and software follow-mode are unavailable on recorded channels.",
    "Wave/Noise and known CH1 LFO carrier keys use that selected reference channel. DDA transient DAC codes are not reconstructed into keyboard PCM; its hardware level and balance remain editable. Unknown Wave RAM is blank and cannot accept a guessed partial stroke; explicit complete replacement is allowed when control is known.",
    "Later VGM control/Wave writes revoke hand gate ownership even when their bytes are unchanged. Frequency writes revoke only manual pitch ownership. Old keyup/Pitch reset and blur cleanup cannot undo later song gates or frequencies.",
    "Independent manualEpoch fences Pause/Resume, Seek, source-validation start/failure/replacement, Stop, Code and disposal. Nonfatal Live errors disable manual helpers without preventing Pause/Seek/new Load.",
    "After a manual mutation, that run permanently stops adding original-song checkpoints. Existing clean points remain usable. Seek restores original native/parser/PCM/Live state; Cancel retains the previous edited run and buffered PCM with hand keys released.",
    "Synth view keeps the authored instrument fully editable/playable alongside the reference, including Software Envelope and DDA loading. Code and VGM stay exclusive. Paused private audition/Capture and channel output flags remain intact.",
    "The same readable standalone ZIP passes new VGM/manual and all nine existing suites on Chromium/WebKit. Playback controls and layout remain compact at1240/390."
  ],
